  "summary": "Recent preprints test corroboration rules, enrichment backgrounds and enhancer-anchored evidence against established driver and GWAS benchmarks.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the explicit grounding of computational genomic inference in reference and evidence choices. Orchestra composes two bioinformatics MCP servers into a LangGraph workflow and finds that requiring agreement of 2 of 4 evidence sources predicts IntOGen driver genes. A background-focused study shows that GO Biological Process enrichment results shift with genome versus exome background in GWAS and WES gene lists. EnSEMBLE pairs gene-level pathway enrichment with enhancer-RNA evidence from standard RNA-seq, cutting redundant signatures by over 97%. AlphaGenome deletion responses are evaluated against chromatin-based baselines for enhancer-gene prediction in primary human astrocytes, and RegTrust-XAI adds trust scoring to CNN chromatin accessibility models. A permutation-free family-wise error approach addresses inflation in moderated top-gene scans under gene correlation. What is new is methodological: corroboration, background control and trust calibration rather than new biological findings. The published Mendelian randomization reappraisal flags a CD40-locus B-cell signal as exploratory, not causal.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
